<title>SINGAPORE: Omni Mold 96 net profit drop 8 percent.</title>
<headline>Omni Mold 96 net profit drop 8 percent.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				1.07 vs  1.16</p>
<p>    Dividend (percent)		    5.00 vs  7.50</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		     1.50 vs  1.60</p>
<p>    Turnover				 17.29 vs 16.84</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	 0.19 vs  0.23</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		    0.35 vs  0.22</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)		1.74 vs  1.63</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			  1.07 vs  1.52</p>
<p>    Tax					 nil  vs  0.36</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries		(loss) 0.07 vs  0.34 (gain)</p>
<p>Note - Omni Mold Ltd is involved in mould-making and injection moulding activities.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
